From: Joe Downing <joedow@google.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] [M156] [remoting] Handle StreamPacketSocket errors and
 close events safely

Original change's description:
> [remoting] Handle StreamPacketSocket errors and close events safely
>
> Updates StreamPacketSocket to align with the webrtc::AsyncPacketSocket
> contract when underlying stream operations fail or callbacks re-enter:
>
> - Defer NotifyClosed() to a posted task and cancel pending close
>   notifications on Close() or destruction.
> - Return -1 from Send() when a synchronous write fails before the
>   packet is written, and reject zero-size packed packets.
> - Serialize re-entrant DoWrite() calls across NotifySentPacket() and
>   NotifyReadyToSend(), check socket_ and send_pending_ in the write
>   loop to avoid overlapping writes, and only fire NotifyReadyToSend()
>   once the send queue is drained.
> - Check a WeakPtr and socket state after each observer notification to
>   detect re-entrant Close() or destruction, and stop processing
>   buffered read data in that case.
> - Unconditionally update the read buffer offset after unpacking
>   complete packets, preventing duplicate packet delivery and ~4 KB per
>   read buffer growth when a read ends on a packet boundary.
> - Add SEQUENCE_CHECKER assertions across StreamPacketSocket entry
>   points.
>
> Test: remoting_unittests --gtest_filter=StreamPacketSocketTest.*
